XPath Injection leading to Information Disclosure and Authentication Bypass The plan describes constructing an XPath query string by directly embedding user-supplied 'username' and 'password' without proper sanitization or parameterization. This allows an attacker to inject malicious XPath fragments, altering the query logic to bypass authentication or extract arbitrary data from the XML document.

